  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "5951178",
      "title": "Why Unit Tests?",
      "lectureOrder": 725,
      "videoOrder": 666,
      "sourceHash": "f68aeb98f9703af3e6531ad8b7100212b4c4b0b5a742994cad96ff96ade4457b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.23,
          "end": 3.6,
          "en": "-: Why might you want to create unit tests?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 5.25,
          "en": "Let's have a look at this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.25,
          "end": 6.72,
          "en": "We get a user component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.72,
          "end": 8.13,
          "en": "We get a user detail component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 8.13,
          "end": 10.86,
          "en": "a reverse pipe, and a user service.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 10.86,
          "end": 12.66,
          "en": "Well, the user component also uses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 12.66,
          "end": 15.33,
          "en": "some input binding heroes and property binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 15.33,
          "end": 17.34,
          "en": "with the user detail component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 17.34,
          "end": 19.17,
          "en": "We can ask a couple of questions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 19.17,
          "end": 21.78,
          "en": "or one of the same question actually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 21.78,
          "end": 23.52,
          "en": "Does the component work as intended?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 23.52,
          "end": 25.59,
          "en": "The pipe and the service?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 25.59,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "This is what we want to answer with unit tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "We also might want to answer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 31.89,
          "en": "does the input work as intended?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 31.89,
          "end": 34.74,
          "en": "Or does the injection work as intended?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 34.74,
          "end": 38.19,
          "en": "These are questions we want to cover with unit tests.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 38.19,
          "end": 40.26,
          "en": "And with unit tests, we hopefully get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 40.26,
          "end": 42.84,
          "en": "a true response for all our tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 42.84,
          "end": 45.6,
          "en": "telling us that our application is working as intended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 45.6,
          "end": 47.46,
          "en": "Of course, you can already imagine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 47.46,
          "end": 50.94,
          "en": "that writing the task correctly is an important part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 50.94,
          "end": 53.07,
          "en": "in order to get the right answers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 53.07,
          "end": 55.26,
          "en": "And that's something I'm not going to teach you here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 55.26,
          "end": 56.94,
          "en": "because I can't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 56.94,
          "end": 59.34,
          "en": "Writing correct tests is again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 59.34,
          "end": 61.05,
          "en": "something for its own course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 61.05,
          "end": 63.24,
          "en": "Not even an Angular 2 specific course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 63.24,
          "end": 65.28,
          "en": "a course focusing on testing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 65.28,
          "end": 67.32,
          "en": "It's not the goal of what I want to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 67.32,
          "end": 69.51,
          "en": "I want to show you how to use testing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 69.51,
          "end": 71.16,
          "en": "in an Angular 2 application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 71.16,
          "end": 74.67,
          "en": "not philosophy about how testing should work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 74.67,
          "end": 76.92,
          "en": "or how tests should be written.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 76.92,
          "end": 79.71000000000001,
          "en": "So with the answers to our questions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 79.71000000000001,
          "end": 83.07,
          "en": "the cool thing is unit tests allow us to guard",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 83.07,
          "end": 85.74,
          "en": "against breaking changes because we could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 85.74,
          "end": 88.23,
          "en": "upon upgrading our Angular 2 application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 88.23,
          "end": 92.25,
          "en": "we rerun all our tests and we see which tests now fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 92.25,
          "end": 94.92,
          "en": "If we know they work before we know which places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 94.92,
          "end": 97.77000000000001,
          "en": "in our application now are broken due to the update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 97.77000000000001,
          "end": 100.35,
          "en": "We can also analyze our code behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 100.35,
          "end": 103.53,
          "en": "to detect both expected and unexpected results",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 103.53,
          "end": 105.96000000000001,
          "en": "and we can reveal design mistakes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 105.96000000000001,
          "end": 108,
          "en": "Maybe when writing our test,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 108,
          "end": 110.49000000000001,
          "en": "we experience some problem writing it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 110.49000000000001,
          "end": 113.25,
          "en": "'cause we find a mistake in our general design",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 113.25,
          "end": 115.02000000000001,
          "en": "or we find it whilst running the test",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 115.02000000000001,
          "end": 117.33,
          "en": "due to an unexpected response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 117.33,
          "end": 118.97999999999999,
          "en": "So this is where tests can help us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 118.97999999999999,
          "end": 121.62,
          "en": "Again, the philosophy behind testing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 121.62,
          "end": 123.24,
          "en": "and how to write correct tests is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 123.24,
          "end": 124.74,
          "en": "something which will not be covered here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 124.74,
          "end": 126.24,
          "en": "which can't be covered here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 128.76,
          "en": "But I want to show you how to create tests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 128.76,
          "end": 130.473,
          "en": "in your Angular 2 application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
